BT 1 0 0 1 0 57 Tm /F2 12 Tf 13.8 TL 1.159971 Tw (Student A: datasets of 50 and 5,000 host-port records were generated and the baseline \(a) Tj T* 0 Tw .855439 Tw (per-line grep loop\) timed with the shell time builtin \(run /usr/bin/time -v the same way to) Tj T* 0 Tw 1.196584 Tw (also record memory\). Student B: the bottleneck is process creation, about three forks per) Tj T* 0 Tw .259439 Tw (line \(echo, grep, grep\), roughly 15,000 forks for 5,000 rows; the refinement is a single awk) Tj T* 0 Tw (pass \(clean_ports\). Correctness check: the two outputs are identical \(cmp\).) Tj T* ET
